WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.812
Broadcasting allows NumPy to combine arrays with different but compatible shapes.

00:00:05.812 --> 00:00:09.927
The simplest example is adding a single number to an array.

00:00:09.927 --> 00:00:13.628
That one number is automatically applied to every element.

00:00:14.194 --> 00:00:20.496
Broadcasting can also apply a one-dimensional array across the rows of a two-dimensional array.

00:00:20.496 --> 00:00:28.666
For example, if each column has a different adjustment value, NumPy can apply those adjustments across many rows

00:00:28.666 --> 00:00:31.116
without manually repeating them.

00:00:31.116 --> 00:00:39.551
Broadcasting is convenient, but incompatible shapes can cause errors or produce results you did not intend.

00:00:39.551 --> 00:00:45.918
When something looks wrong, inspect the shapes of both arrays before trying to fix the calculation.
